course: dictionary
lesson: 68
title: Acne
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Acne is a skin condition. It causes spots, blackheads and pimples, mostly on the face, back and chest. It is a noun, and it has no plural, so you say acne, not acnes.
explain: Why does it happen? During the teenage years, hormones change, and the skin makes more oil. This oil can block tiny holes in the skin called pores, and spots form. Many teenagers have acne, so it is common, and it is not a sign that anything is wrong with you.
explain: Context gives clues. «Steroids are not protein; they can damage the heart and liver, cause bad acne and mood swings, and in teenagers stop growth early.» Bad acne is listed with other harmful effects, so acne is a skin problem that can be serious and upsetting. Kind words matter, because teasing about spots hurts.
fact: Acne is a skin condition that causes spots, blackheads and pimples.
fact: Acne is most common on the face, back and chest.
fact: Acne is very common in teenagers, and it happens when hormones change and the skin makes more oil.
fact: «Acne cream» is a cream you put on the skin to help acne. A doctor or pharmacist can help you choose one.
fact: Teasing someone about their spots is unkind, and it hurts.
exercise: Where does acne most often appear on the body? | *The face, back and chest | The knees and toes | The hair | The ears only
exercise: «Steroids can cause bad acne and mood swings.» In this sentence, what is acne? | A type of food | *A skin problem with spots | A kind of medicine | A feeling of being sad
exercise: Maya says acne is only for adults. What is the true fact? | Acne only happens to babies | *Acne is very common in teenagers | Acne cannot be treated | Acne is a kind of bone
test: What makes the skin produce more oil in teenagers? | Eating too many carrots | Too much sunshine | *Changes in hormones | Cold weather
test: Who can give help with acne? | A football coach | *A doctor or a pharmacist | A bus driver
exam: Which is the kindest thing to do for a classmate with acne? | *Be kind, because teasing about spots hurts | Tease them about their spots | Tell everyone about it
